# Example backend settings. You usually don't need a .env at all: the defaults
# in coboltutor/backend/src/coboltutor_backend/config.py run Granite 4.2 8B on a
# local Ollama, and Docker Compose sets its own values.
#
# To override settings when running the backend directly (`uv run coboltutor-backend`),
# copy this file to coboltutor/backend/.env (the backend reads .env from the
# directory it's started in) and uncomment what you need. .env files are
# gitignored; never commit one.
#
# Every setting needs the COBOLTUTOR_ prefix; the backend ignores names without it.
# For ready-made sets of values, see coboltutor/backend/profiles/:
#   local-ollama.conf  - Granite 4.2 8B on Ollama (local development)
#   cluster-vllm.conf  - Granite 4.2 30B on vLLM (HPC cluster; docs/cluster-support.md)

# Where the model server's OpenAI-compatible API is.
# COBOLTUTOR_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Model name as the server knows it (Ollama tag, or vLLM's --served-model-name).
# COBOLTUTOR_LLM_MODEL=granite4.2:8b

# Only needed for servers that check it (vLLM with an API key). Put the real
# key here only in your own uncommitted .env, never in this example file.
# COBOLTUTOR_LLM_API_KEY=

# none | low | medium | high, or empty to leave it out of requests.
# COBOLTUTOR_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
